-- title:
--   Hecke-pinned λ-adic eigenplane in the Tate module of J₀(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the sense of [`CuspForm.IsNewform`](def/CuspForm_Newforms.html#L23) (a normalised eigenform none of whose good eigensystems occurs at a proper divisor of $M$), let $\lambda$ be a prime, and let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing $\lambda$ and every prime divisor of $M$. Let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb{C}$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (↑S \ {lam})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the corresponding Hecke generators, satisfying $\chi_g(T_\ell)=$ the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ to $O'$. Then there is a type $O''$ carrying the same structures (characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field), an $O'$-algebra structure making it module-finite over $O'$ with $O'\to O''$ a local homomorphism and injective, together with a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra structure, such that for every fraction field $K$ of $O''$ the following holds. Equip $J_0(M)$, the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with its `HeckeAlg = MvPolynomial Nat.Primes ℤ` module structure `heckeModuleBar M`, let $T=$ [`ModularCurve.TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/ModularCurve_EichlerShimuraData.html#L15) be the submodule of sequences $x:\mathbb{N}\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$, and let a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ be given whose scalar multiplication is coordinatewise via reduction $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda\to\mathbb{Z}/\lambda^n$. Let $\rho_M$ be a monoid homomorphism from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $O''$-endomorphisms of $O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T$ with $\rho_M(\sigma)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes y$ whenever $y=\sigma\cdot x$ coordinatewise, and let $T_M$ be a ring homomorphism from `HeckeAlg` to the same endomorphism ring with $T_M(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$. Then there is a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ with $\dim_K W=2$, stable under the base change to $K$ of every $\rho_M(\sigma)$, such that: for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, the base change of $T_M$ of the generator at $\ell$ acts on $W$ as the scalar obtained by mapping $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ into $K$, and for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field, the trace on $W$ of the restriction of the base change of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ equals that same scalar; moreover the generator at $\lambda$ acts on $W$ by the image of $\iota(\chi_g(T_\lambda))$ if $\lambda\nmid M$, and by the image of $\iota(\chi_g(U_\lambda))$ if $\lambda\mid M$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two newform, realised as a two-dimensional Galois-stable eigenplane in the Tate module of $J_0(M)$, with the Hecke operator at $\lambda$ itself ($T_\lambda$ or $U_\lambda$ according to whether $\lambda$ divides the level) pinned to act by the corresponding eigenvalue; no assertion is made about the local behaviour of the plane at $\lambda$. It is used in the passage to ordinariness, namely by [`CuspForm.isOrdinaryAt_of_point_of_isUnit_up_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible_of_residual_isOrdinaryAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.isOrdinaryAt_of_point_of_isUnit_up_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible_of_residual_isOrdinaryAt).
